        "title": "Continental Interiors - Lewis+Clark, Livingstone+Stanley, Burke+Wills, Younghusband",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "1804–06 ─── LEWIS+CLARK: Missouri → Pacific. US Corps of Discovery.\n  1841–73 ─── LIVINGSTONE: Africa. Three major expeditions.\n              Source of the Nile. Anti-slavery. Christian missions.\n  1860–61 ─── BURKE+WILLS: Melbourne to Gulf of Carpentaria. Both died.\n  1871   ─── STANLEY: \"Dr. Livingstone, I presume?\"\n  1874–77 ─── STANLEY: Congo River to its mouth.\n  1887–91 ─── YOUNGHUSBAND: Crossing of Gobi Desert; Mustagh Pass.\n```"
